        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-15T22:36:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aren\u0027t the members of this struct placed in the stack anyway? How does it help reduce the stack depth?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e4589b1a89b2b1616006af3c481c90da557cb5f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e7a6317_e56cebea",
        "filename": "include/i2c.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-15T23:15:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the calling convention, we are passing in only pointer to the structure as a parameter instead of actually copying individual variables as parameters in the stack frame.",
      "parentUuid": "5808139d_9f7260d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e4589b1a89b2b1616006af3c481c90da557cb5f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c226e0b_ac11fe8c",
        "filename": "include/i2c.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-16T23:19:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The call stack of functions inside i2c_xfer() is several calls deep, in a way that doesn\u0027t lend itself to tail chaining.  So currently the params are all pushed onto the stack several times.",
      "parentUuid": "0e7a6317_e56cebea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 131,
